    "q-5241": {
      "dom_id": "step-q5241",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Find the $5$th term of the following geometric sequence.\n\n$$\n2,\\,-4,\\,8,\\,-16,\\,…\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14204584/assets/7c6697d2a70a7499e6a834f3e588257c88f5da433c7365b9b1777314377e122d.png)\n\nNotice that the sequence is geometric, with a common ratio of \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{(-4)}{2}=-2.\n$$\n\nSo, we can get each term by multiplying the previous term by $-2.$\n\nContinuing to list terms of the sequence until we get to the $5$th term, we obtain the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14204584/assets/a5cd75c3e262f76d12da48cd8e86bf04b2532f7e7084d1968ac30bd103373f64.png)\n\nTherefore, the $5$th term is $32.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
