    "q-101241": {
      "dom_id": "step-q101241",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Given that $50$, $5x$, and $12.5x$ are the first three terms of a geometric sequence, find $x.$",
      "worked_solution": "The first three terms are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}=50,\\,{a}_{2}=5x,\\,{a}_{3}=12.5x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe common ratio of the first two terms is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{5x}{50}=\\frac{x}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, the common ratio of the second and third terms is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{3}}{{a}_{2}}=\\frac{12.5x}{5x}=2.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by equating the values for $r$ and solving for $x,$ we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2.5 & =\\frac{x}{10} \\\\ 25 & =x \\\\ x & =25.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
