      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Given that $8$, $6x$, and $10x$ are the first three terms of a geometric sequence, find $x.$",
      "worked_solution": "The first three terms are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}=8,\\,{a}_{2}=6x,\\,{a}_{3}=10x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe common ratio of the first two terms is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{6x}{8}=\\frac{3x}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, the common ratio of the second and third terms is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{3}}{{a}_{2}}=\\frac{10x}{6x}=\\frac{5}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by equating the values for $r$ and solving for $x,$ we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3x}{4} & =\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ 3x & =\\frac{20}{3} \\\\ x & =\\frac{20}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
